1
00:00:03,230 --> 00:00:06,203
The banner appears when Paced Dialing is on.

2
00:00:06,203 --> 00:00:08,285
Here it says Nothing due yet:

3
00:00:08,285 --> 00:00:12,745
records wait, but the latest pacing cycle found none it may dial now.

4
00:00:12,745 --> 00:00:16,968
A green banner says the dialer is active and placing calls, and a

5
00:00:16,968 --> 00:00:19,050
blue one says it is starting.

6
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:22,431
Amber means attention.

7
00:00:22,431 --> 00:00:26,312
Dialer idle says work is due but no agent is available.

8
00:00:26,312 --> 00:00:32,166
Dialer holding back says the abandonment policy, the compliance check or calls already

9
00:00:32,166 --> 00:00:34,520
in flight keep it from dialing.

10
00:00:35,270 --> 00:00:36,538
Red means act.

11
00:00:36,538 --> 00:00:42,181
Dialer stalled says due work is waiting and no cycle completed for several minutes.

12
00:00:42,181 --> 00:00:48,267
Dialer not pacing says the pacing lock has not been acquired, so every cycle skips itself.

13
00:00:48,267 --> 00:00:53,340
Both need your administrator, who checks the distributed lock and the log.

